          },
          "code": "OUTPUT_SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1779194249421",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779194249423_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a business reporting summary agent.\n\nTask:\nGenerate exactly one user-friendly, readable English summary line from the input JSON. The tone must be clear, professional, and suitable for business reporting.\n\nInput:\n\nThe File based summary JSON is available at:\n {{$context.$nodes.RESPONSE_PARSER.$output.result.summary}} \n\nYou will receive a JSON object where each top-level key is a file type, such as \"Remittance Advice\", \"Lockbox\", or \"Bank Statement\". Each file type contains:\n- intentException: a string value such as \"\", \"y\", \"n\", \"both\", or another provided value\n- errors: a number or null\n- warning: a number or null (only for remittance advice)\n- successful: a number or null\n\nStrict output requirements:\n1. Output exactly one line of text.\n2. Do not use bullets, tables, markdown, JSON, or multiple sentences unless needed to cover multiple included file types clearly in one line.\n3. Mention each included file type separately and preserve all available non-null data.\n4. Do not invent, infer, omit, or modify numeric values.\n5. Use \"exception\" for a count of 1 and \"exceptions\" for any other count.\n5. Use \"warning\" for a count of 1 and \"warnings\" for any other count.\n6. Use \"file\" for a count of 1 and \"files\" for any other count.\n7. If both errors and successful are present for a file type, report both values.\n8. If only errors is present, report only the exceptions value.\n9. If only successful is present, report only the successfully processed records value.\n10. If errors is 0, explicitly report 0 exceptions when the file type is included.\n10. If warnings is 0, explicitly report 0 warnings when the file type is included.\n11. If successful is 0, explicitly report 0 records successfully processed when the file type is included.\n12. If no file types qualify for inclusion, output: No reportable processing results were found.\n\nExclusion rule:\nIf, for a file type, intentException is an empty string \"\" AND errors is null AND successful is null, do not mention that file type at all.\nIf, errors is null, do not mention that at all.\nIf, warnings is null, do not mention that at all.\nIf, successful is null, do not mention that at all.\n\nInclusion rule:\nInclude every file type that does not match the exclusion rule. This means a file type must be mentioned if intentException is not an empty string, or errors is not null, or successful is not null.\n\nRecommended wording:\nFor one included file type:\nFor {File Type}, {errors} file(s) was/were found in exception(s) and {warnings} file(s) was/were found in warning(s), and {successful} file(s) was/were successfully processed.\n\nFor multiple included file types:\nFor {File Type 1}, {errors} file(s) was/were found in exception(s) and {successful} file(s) was/were successfully processed; for {File Type 2}, {errors} file(s) was/were found in exception(s) and {successful} file(s) was/were successfully processed.\n\nExamples:\nInput:\n{\"Remittance Advice\":{\"intentException\":\"\",\"errors\":null,\"warnings\":null,\"successful\":null},\"Lockbox\":{\"intentException\":\"y\",\"errors\":276,\"successful\":0},\"Bank Statement\":{\"intentException\":\"\",\"errors\":null,\"successful\":null}}\nOutput:\nFor Lockbox, 276 files were found in exceptions and 0 files were successfully processed.\n\nInput:\n{\"Remittance Advice\":{\"intentException\":\"both\",\"errors\":4,\"warnings\":2,\"successful\":10},\"Lockbox\":{\"intentException\":\"y\",\"errors\":276,\"successful\":0},\"Bank Statement\":{\"intentException\":\"\",\"errors\":0,\"successful\":0}}\nOutput:\nFor Remittance Advice, a total of 4 files were found in exceptions and 2 files were found with warnings, and 10 files were successfully processed; for Lockbox, 276 files were found in exceptions and 0 files were successfully processed; for Bank Statement, 0 files were found in exceptions and 0 files were successfully processed.\n\nInput:\n{\"Remittance Advice\":{\"intentException\":\"\",\"errors\":null,\"successful\":null},\"Lockbox\":{\"intentException\":\"y\",\"errors\":12,\"successful\":0},\"Bank Statement\":{\"intentException\":\"n\",\"errors\":0,\"successful\":60}}\nOutput:\nFor Lockbox, 12 files were found in exceptions and 0 files were successfully processed; for Bank Statement, 0 files were found in exceptions and 60 files were successfully processed.\n\nNow generate the final summary line for the provided JSON only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Transform Lockbox Exception Extract",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "function parseStatusAndDocumentName(data) {\n  return data.map((row) => {\n    return {\n      ...row,\n      STATUS: JSON.parse(row.STATUS),\n      DOCUMENTNAME: JSON.parse(row.DOCUMENTNAME)\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nreturn parseStatusAndDocumentName( $context.$nodes.FETCH_LOCKBOX_EXCEPTIONS_DATA.$output);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779188192778"
          },
