          "code": "LOCKBOX_FILTER_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1780494743834",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780494743835_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Lockbox Filter Clause Prompt\n\nYou are a generic filter-clause extraction engine for Oracle ERP Lockbox customer payment file inquiries.\n\nInput:\n\n```text\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n```\n\nYour job is to read the user's message and return exactly one plain text filter clause.\n\nReturn only the plain text filter clause.\nDo not return JSON.\nDo not return a JSON object.\nDo not return a JSON array.\nDo not return a JSON string.\nDo not wrap the output in quotes.\nDo not explain anything.\nDo not add markdown.\nDo not ask follow-up questions.\n\nThis prompt is for Lockbox flow routing only. Do not use Lockbox, file type, source type, exception, status, customer, amount, currency, or any other domain context to construct the filter. Only extract supported filters from the user input.\n\n--------------------------------\nOUTPUT SHAPE\n--------------------------------\n\nReturn exactly one plain text response.\n\nSupported single-filter forms:\n\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat')\n```\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated > sysdate - N\n```\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)\n```\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated < sysdate - N\n```\n\nSupported combined-filter form:\n\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat', 'LBX_20240801.dat') AND timeCreated > sysdate - N\n```\n\nIf no supported filter is found, return an empty response with no characters. Do not return quotes, `\"\"`, or any placeholder.\n\n--------------------------------\nSUPPORTED FILTERS\n--------------------------------\n\nOnly these filters are supported:\n\n1. Exact one-or-more document/file name filter using `transmissionName`\n2. Recent-day filter using `timeCreated`\n3. Today filter using `timeCreated`\n4. Older-than day filter using `timeCreated`\n\nDo not create any other filter.\n\n--------------------------------\nDOCUMENT NAME FILTER RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nCreate a document-name filter when the user asks about one or more specific files or documents.\n\nUse this exact format:\n\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('DOCUMENT_NAME')\n```\n\nFor multiple file names, use this exact format:\n\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('DOCUMENT_NAME_1', 'DOCUMENT_NAME_2')\n```\n\nRules:\n\n1. Use only the exact column name `transmissionName`.\n2. Extract every exact file/document name from the user input.\n3. Preserve each file/document name case, numbers, separators, and extension exactly as written by the user.\n4. Include the full extension when present, such as `.xml`, `.dat`, `.txt`, `.csv`, `.zip`, `.pgp`, `.gpg`, `.bai`, or `.mt940`.\n5. Remove surrounding user quotes from extracted values, but keep the content inside the quotes exactly.\n6. Wrap each extracted value in single quotes.\n7. If a file/document name contains a single quote, escape it by doubling it.\n8. Always start the filter value with a leading space followed by `AND`.\n9. Use `in (...)` for both one file name and multiple file names.\n10. If multiple file names are present, include them comma-separated in the order they appear in the user input.\n11. If the same file name appears more than once, include it once.\n\nRecognize document/file-name phrases such as:\n\n- in file `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- for file `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- file `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- file named `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- file name `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- filename `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- document `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- document named `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- document name `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- with document `LBX_20240731.dat`\n- for document `LBX_20240731.dat`\n\nExamples:\n\n- show lockbox exception in file LBX_20240731.dat -> ` AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat')`\n- show status for lockbox document lockbox-west-004.pgp -> ` AND transmissionName in ('lockbox-west-004.pgp')`\n- did lockbox file LBX_ACH_0724.txt load -> ` AND transmissionName in ('LBX_ACH_0724.txt')`\n- show errors for filename lockbox_2024_07_31.zip -> ` AND transmissionName in ('lockbox_2024_07_31.zip')`\n- show details for file \"Lockbox West July 005.dat\" -> ` AND transmissionName in ('Lockbox West July 005.dat')`\n- show files LBX_20240731.dat and LBX_20240801.dat -> ` AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat', 'LBX_20240801.dat')`\n\n--------------------------------\nTIME FILTER RULES\n--------------------------------\n\nThe only supported time filters are `timeCreated` filters for numeric recent-day periods, today, and numeric older-than day periods.\n\nUse one of these exact formats:\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated > sysdate - N\n```\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)\n```\n\n```text\n AND timeCreated < sysdate - N\n```\n\nRules:\n\n1. Create a recent-day filter when the user mentions a relative day period with a numeric value, such as `last N days`, `past N days`, or `previous N days`.\n2. For recent-day filters, extract the number as `N` and return ` AND timeCreated > sysdate - N`.\n3. Create a today filter when the user says `today`.\n4. For today filters, return ` AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)`.\n5. Create an older-than filter when the user says `older than N days`.\n6. For older-than filters, extract the number as `N` and return ` AND timeCreated < sysdate - N`.\n7. Use only the exact column name `timeCreated`.\n8. Always start the filter value with a leading space followed by `AND`.\n9. Do not create time filters for yesterday, this week, this month, dates, date ranges, months, years, or written-out numbers such as `seven`.\n10. Do not use `BETWEEN`.\n11. Do not invent a default day range.\n\nExamples:\n\n- last 7 days -> ` AND timeCreated > sysdate - 7`\n- past 30 days -> ` AND timeCreated > sysdate - 30`\n- previous 5 days -> ` AND timeCreated > sysdate - 5`\n- in the last 10 days -> ` AND timeCreated > sysdate - 10`\n- today -> ` AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)`\n- older than 7 days -> ` AND timeCreated < sysdate - 7`\n\n--------------------------------\nCOMBINING FILTERS\n--------------------------------\n\nIf the user input contains both one supported document-name filter with one or more names and one supported time filter, return both filters in this order:\n\n1. `transmissionName`\n2. `timeCreated`\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox exception in file LBX_20240731.dat for last 7 days\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat') AND timeCreated > sysdate - 7\n```\n\nIf the user input contains only one supported filter, return only that filter.\n\nIf the user input contains multiple different file or document names, include all recognized names in the `transmissionName in (...)` filter.\n\nIf the user input contains multiple different time filters and no single whole-request time filter can be determined, return an empty response with no characters.\n\n--------------------------------\nDO NOT DO THESE\n--------------------------------\n\n- Do not return a JSON object.\n- Do not return a JSON array.\n- Do not return keys.\n- Do not return null.\n- Do not return unsupported filters.\n- Do not create filters for source type, exception status, processing status, amount, currency, customer, bank, account, batch, transmission status, import status, or any attribute other than `transmissionName` and `timeCreated`.\n- Do not infer a document name from ordinary words unless the user clearly identifies a file or document.\n- Do not infer a time filter from vague time expressions.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions.\n- Do not output anything except the plain text filter clause. If no filter is supported, output nothing.\n\n--------------------------------\nEXAMPLES\n--------------------------------\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox exception in file LBX_20240731.dat\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat')\n```\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox status for document lockbox-west-004.pgp\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('lockbox-west-004.pgp')\n```\n\nInput:\ndid lockbox file LBX_ACH_0724.txt load today\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_ACH_0724.txt') AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)\n```\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox errors for file lockbox_2024_07_31.zip in the past 10 days\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('lockbox_2024_07_31.zip') AND timeCreated > sysdate - 10\n```\n\nInput:\nshow records for lockbox file LBX_20240731.dat older than 30 days\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat') AND timeCreated < sysdate - 30\n```\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox status for last 7 days\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND timeCreated > sysdate - 7\n```\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox status today\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND timeCreated >= trunc(sysdate)\n```\n\nInput:\nshow lockbox status yesterday\n\nOutput:\n```text\n```\n\nInput:\nshow file LBX_20240731.dat and file LBX_20240801.dat\n\nOutput:\n```text\n AND transmissionName in ('LBX_20240731.dat', 'LBX_20240801.dat')\n```\n\n--------------------------------\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n--------------------------------\n\nRead:\n\n```text\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n```\n\nReturn exactly one plain text response:\n\n- A `transmissionName` filter when the input contains one or more supported exact file/document names.\n- A `timeCreated` filter when the input contains one supported time period.\n- A combined `transmissionName` and `timeCreated` filter when both are present.\n- Empty output with no characters when no supported filter is present or when a single valid filter clause cannot be determined."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Add Lockbox Filter Clause",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const LockboxObj = $context.$nodes.CHECK_LOCKBOX.$output.result ;\n\nLockboxObj.filterClause = $context.$nodes.LOCKBOX_FILTER_GENERATOR.$output ;\n\nreturn LockboxObj;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779117222323"
          },
          "code": "ADD_LOCKBOX_FILTER_CLAUSE",
          "id": "1780494770830",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Out of Scope Handler"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1780929502250",
            "false": "add_false_1780929360113"
          },
          "code": "OUT_OF_SCOPE_HANDLER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1779114436318",
          "id": "1780929360113",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780929360114_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.UserIntent[0].sourceType == 'Out of Scope'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
